{
  "body" : "Create an original anime character drawing with a naive, childlike, rough hand-drawn aesthetic.\n\nCHARACTER\n- Main character: {{character}}\n- Additional notes: {{extra}}\n\nCORE STYLE\n- The image should look like a simple handmade anime drawing created with crayons, oil pastels, colored pencils, or chunky digital brushes.\n- The drawing must feel naive, spontaneous, playful, and slightly clumsy rather than professionally illustrated.\n- Use simplified anime forms and exaggerated cartoon-like features instead of realistic human anatomy.\n- Keep the character cute and expressive, but avoid realistic facial structure, realistic skin, or realistic body proportions.\n- The drawing should have the visual simplicity and charm of a child's drawing while still clearly reading as an anime character.\n\nLINEWORK\n- Use thick, rough, irregular hand-drawn lines.\n- Lines should wobble, overlap, break, and vary noticeably in thickness.\n- Use a small number of broad strokes rather than many precise lines.\n- Allow construction marks, accidental strokes, overshooting lines, and imperfect contours to remain visible.\n- Do not carefully clean up the drawing.\n- Do not use delicate or precise ink lines.\n- Do not create professional manga line art.\n- The outline should feel drawn quickly by hand rather than carefully traced.\n\nCOLORING\n- Use broad, chunky areas of color with visible crayon, oil pastel, or rough brush texture.\n- Color should be applied unevenly, with obvious streaks, gaps, overlaps, and changes in opacity.\n- Let some strokes extend outside the character's contours.\n- Do not carefully fill every region.\n- Avoid smooth digital fills and perfectly controlled color boundaries.\n- Use only a small number of muted colors.\n- Colors should feel dusty, soft, slightly faded, and imperfect rather than vibrant or glossy.\n- Prefer muted pink, dusty red, faded blue, lavender, gray, cream, and warm off-white tones.\n\nFORM AND DETAIL\n- Keep anatomy and clothing highly simplified.\n- Reduce complex forms to a few broad shapes.\n- Use simple, cartoon-like facial features.\n- Avoid realistic eyes, realistic skin texture, realistic hair rendering, or detailed anatomy.\n- Do not add fine wrinkles, individual hair strands, delicate shading, or intricate textures.\n- Large visual shapes and rough marks should dominate the image.\n- The character should feel more like a charming drawing than a finished illustration.\n\nSHADING\n- Use almost no realistic shading.\n- When shading is needed, use one or two rough blocks of color.\n- Shading should look like another quick crayon or brush stroke rather than modeled light and shadow.\n- Avoid gradients, soft airbrushing, glossy highlights, and realistic volume.\n\nBACKGROUND\n- Use a plain white or warm off-white background.\n- Leave large areas completely empty.\n- A few crude hand-drawn decorative marks, doodles, hearts, stars, flowers, or handwritten notes may appear if appropriate.\n- Background elements must be simple and secondary.\n\nOVERALL IMPRESSION\n- Naive\n- Childlike\n- Rough\n- Cute\n- Playful\n- Handmade\n- Simplified\n- Slightly messy\n- Colorful but muted\n- Clearly hand-drawn\n\nThe final result should NOT look like a polished anime illustration that has been given a sketch filter. It should look like the illustration was originally drawn this way from the beginning: simple, rough, chunky, imperfect, childlike, and handmade.\n\nSIGNATURE\n- Include \"{{signature}}\" as a small handwritten artist signature.\n- The signature should look casually handwritten with an imperfect hand-drawn stroke.\n- Place it naturally in an area of empty space, preferably near a lower corner.\n- Never render it as a typed font, logo, title, or polished typography.\n\nAVOID\n- Realistic human proportions\n- Realistic faces\n- Realistic skin\n- Realistic lighting\n- Professional portrait illustration\n- Detailed anime rendering\n- Highly polished digital painting\n- Detailed pencil portraiture\n- Fine ink drawing\n- Clean manga line art\n- Vector outlines\n- Smooth gradients\n- Airbrush shading\n- Glossy rendering\n- Intricate anatomy\n- Detailed hair strands\n- Fine cross-hatching\n- Excessive detail\n- Perfectly controlled coloring\n- Cleanly filled shapes\n- Cinematic composition\n- Photorealism\n\n——————\nCharacter: {{character}}\nAdditional notes: {{extra}}\nHandwritten signature: {{signature}}",
  "community" : {
